azgor wrote:
> This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
> freenode.net.  Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.

Lots of good ideas here.  Some of my 2c:

> [1]: Nudist conduct:  Can be obtained by wearing only one of either
> three non-body armor types (gloves, boots, helmet) at any given time.
> Conduct start is triggered by removing any starting armor (other than
> the allowed) before leaving DL 1. --aristotle73

Why allow any armor?  It's been demonstrated that true nudist conduct
is possible.  Also, stepping off the up-stairs wearing any armor, or
using the W command at all, should immediately break the conduct.

> [3]: Have attacking a water elemental with a towel (or throwing it at
> them) deal major damage --scwizard

I like this one.  Other ideas for towels:
- wearing it on your head not only makes you blind, but reduces damage
from poison gas, stinking cloud, etc.
- attempting to eat it produces "You suck some filth from the towel.
Yummy!" and provides a small amount of nutrition (only allowed every
few hundred turns or so)
- reading it should produce something funny ("Don't Panic", perhaps, or
"Property of Yendorian Hotel")

> [6]: Alternate suggestion to the above: Put a cap on the number of
> bones files that a character can get in a certain number of turns. This
> will stop DfVers from destroying bones files as they dig down.
> --scwizard

Not a bad idea.  Maybe finding a bones file starts a turn counter
during which no more bones can be found.

> [7]: Track "petless" conduct.  Must start with pettype:none, and must
> not tame any monster during the game. --PsyMar

I like it, though this wouldn't be very hard.  Magic traps would have
to be avoided.  Call it "loner" conduct.

> [11]: If you dip a wraith corpse into a potion of holy water, you you
> get a uncursed potion of gain level --scwizard

Too powerful.  Potions of gain level are much better objects than
wraith corpses.

> [12]: Entering an armor store naked has a chance of the shopkeeper
> giving you a free robe. --aristotle73

Too powerful.  Maybe an orcish or dwarvish cloak.

> [15]: A diving helmet.  Combine with an oilskin cloak to go for a walk
> in the moat. --Grunt

I like this idea a lot.  Basically it's a helm of magical breathing
(though "diving helmet" is a better name).  This would quickly become
part of many people's regular AK, though, so maybe it's too powerful.
Would it automatically be rustproof?



